---
/**
 * /course
 *
 * A course is not recorded and has no date. The page says that first, publishes
 * the outline it would follow so a visitor knows what they are joining a list
 * for, and sends them to the five guides that are already written.
 *
 * No runtime, no price, no platform. None of that is decided, and inventing any
 * of it is exactly the failure the claim ledger exists to stop. The outline is
 * held to the same bar as the rest of the site: every lesson names something
 * that exists today, except the builder one, which is marked as not shipped.
 */
import SoonPageLayout from '../components/SoonPageLayout.astro';

/*
  Three titles here read differently from how the feature is usually described,
  and the difference is deliberate. Custom commands land in a collapsed "Other
  actions" menu in the viewer footer, never a toolbar. Hooks are instructions
  the assistant reads, not an engine that runs them. And there is no templates
  lesson, because no template setting is contributed anywhere.
*/
const modules = [
  {
    n: '1',
    title: 'Set up',
    lessons: [
      { title: 'Install both halves', body: 'What the VS Code extension gives you, and what the Spec Kit extension adds on top.' },
      { title: 'Pick your AI provider', body: 'Eleven of them, and what changes when yours cannot submit the prompt for you.' },
      { title: 'Read the sidebar', body: 'Your specs, the status of each one, and the steering docs underneath.' },
    ],
  },
  {
    n: '2',
    title: 'Your first spec',
    lessons: [
      { title: 'Create a spec', body: 'Choosing a workflow, and giving it the images and context it needs.' },
      { title: 'The spec viewer', body: 'The documents, the step rail, and where you are in the run.' },
      { title: 'Run a step, then review it', body: 'Comment on the line you disagree with, and send the notes back with Refine.' },
      { title: 'Read the Overview', body: 'Intent, decisions, coverage, and the run log folded underneath.' },
    ],
  },
  {
    n: '3',
    title: 'Make it yours',
    lessons: [
      { title: 'Add your own actions', body: 'Custom commands, and where they show up in the viewer footer.' },
      { title: 'Attach work around a step', body: 'A companion.yml hook: a shell command, an instruction, or a node file of your own.' },
      { title: 'Write your own workflow', body: 'Your phases, your commands, your output files, offered by Create Spec.' },
    ],
  },
  {
    n: '4',
    title: 'Going further',
    lessons: [
      { title: 'Living specs', body: 'Turning them on, adopting a capability, and keeping it central or beside the code.' },
      { title: 'Drift and coverage', body: 'What each report tells you, and why neither one can ever block a build.' },
      { title: 'The workflow builder', body: 'Not built yet. This lesson arrives with it.', soon: true },
    ],
  },
];

const guides = [
  {
    step: '01',
    title: 'Getting started',
    body: 'Install both halves, create your first spec, run it, and read the record it leaves behind.',
    href: '/docs/start/getting-started/',
  },
  {
    step: '02',
    title: 'Pick a pipeline',
    body: 'Choose stock SpecKit or SpecKit Companion, then bend either one into a workflow of your own.',
    href: '/docs/guides/pick-a-pipeline/',
  },
  {
    step: '03',
    title: 'Review and refine',
    body: 'Comment on a spec line by line, keep the comments in the repo, and hand the pending ones to your AI.',
    href: '/docs/guides/review-and-refine/',
  },
  {
    step: '04',
    title: 'Anatomy of the Overview',
    body: 'How to read the record a finished run leaves behind, and what it will not tell you.',
    href: '/docs/anatomy/anatomy-of-the-overview/',
  },
  {
    step: '05',
    title: 'Living specs',
    body: 'One durable spec per capability, kept next to the code, updated by the runs that change it.',
    href: '/docs/guides/living-specs/',
  },
];
---

<SoonPageLayout
  title="Course"
  description="A course on spec-driven development with SpecKit Companion is not recorded yet. Here is the outline it would follow, the written guides that cover the same ground, and a list to join."
  headline="A course, once there is one worth sitting through"
  standing="Nothing is recorded and there is no date. What follows is the outline it would run, so you know what you would be joining a list for."
  waitlistId="course"
  waitlistNote="Once this list is wired up, an address here gets exactly one message, on the day the thing ships. There is no newsletter behind it."
  pose="reading"
  poseAlt="The SpecKit Companion mascot sitting with an open book, reading."
>
  <p slot="lead">
    The plan is a walkthrough of taking real work through the pipeline end to end: writing the spec,
    reading the plan, reviewing the tasks, and reading the run once it finishes. It has not been
    made, so the honest answer to when is that we do not know.
  </p>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="inner">
      <p class="eyebrow">THE OUTLINE</p>
      <h2>Four parts, from an empty workspace to a spec that outlives the ticket</h2>
      <p class="section-lede">
        This is the shape, not a schedule. Every lesson below covers something the product does
        today, apart from the last one, which waits on the builder.
      </p>

      <ol class="modules">
        {
          modules.map((mod) => (
            <li class="module">
              <p class="module-head">
                <span class="module-n" aria-hidden="true">
                  {mod.n}
                </span>
                <span class="module-title">{mod.title}</span>
              </p>
              <ul class="lessons">
                {mod.lessons.map((lesson) => (
                  <li class="lesson" data-soon={lesson.soon ? '' : undefined}>
                    <span class="lesson-title">
                      {lesson.title}
                      {lesson.soon && <span class="lesson-soon">soon</span>}
                    </span>
                    <span class="lesson-body">{lesson.body}</span>
                  </li>
                ))}
              </ul>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="inner">
      <p class="eyebrow">THE WRITTEN VERSION</p>
      <h2>Five guides cover the same ground today</h2>
      <p class="section-lede">
        Read in this order they walk from an empty workspace to a finished run you can hand to
        someone else.
      </p>

      <ol class="guides">
        {
          guides.map((guide) => (
            <li class="guide">
              <span class="guide-step" aria-hidden="true">
                {guide.step}
              </span>
              <span class="guide-text">
                <a class="guide-title" href={guide.href}>
                  {guide.title}
                </a>
                <span class="guide-body">{guide.body}</span>
              </span>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Fragment slot="back">
    <a href="/docs/start/getting-started/">start with getting started</a>
    <a href="/docs/">all the docs</a>
    <a href="/">back to the landing page</a>
  </Fragment>
</SoonPageLayout>

<style>
  .inner {
    max-width: var(--page-width);
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 0 var(--pad-section-x);
  }

  .section {
    padding: 56px 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }

  .eyebrow {
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-16);
    color: var(--accent);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--fs-mono);
    letter-spacing: var(--ls-eyebrow);
  }

  h2 {
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-12);
    max-width: var(--measure-footer);
    font-size: var(--fs-h2);
    font-weight: var(--fw-black);
    line-height: var(--lh-display);
    letter-spacing: var(--ls-h2-stat);
    text-wrap: balance;
  }

  .section-lede {
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-26);
    max-width: var(--measure-lead);
    color: var(--text-body);
    font-size: var(--fs-body);
    line-height: var(--lh-prose);
  }

  .modules {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: var(--space-24);
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-8);
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }

  .module {
    padding: var(--space-24);
    background: var(--panel);
    border: 1px solid var(--border-panel);
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
  }

  .module-head {
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: var(--space-12);
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-18);
    padding-bottom: var(--space-14);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }

  .module-n {
    flex: none;
    color: var(--accent);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--fs-ui-sm);
  }

  .module-title {
    color: var(--text-primary);
    font-size: var(--fs-h3);
    font-weight: var(--fw-bold);
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  }

  .lessons {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-16);
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }

  .lesson {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-4);
  }

  .lesson-title {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--space-8);
    color: var(--text-primary);
    font-size: var(--fs-body);
    font-weight: var(--fw-bold);
  }

  /* The one lesson that does not describe something shipped has to say so
     on the page, not only in a footnote. */
  .lesson-soon {
    flex: none;
    padding: 2px var(--space-6);
    border: 1px solid var(--border-panel);
    border-radius: 999px;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--fs-chip);
    letter-spacing: var(--ls-eyebrow);
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .lesson[data-soon] .lesson-title {
    color: var(--text-body);
  }

  .lesson-body {
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-size: var(--fs-ui-sm);
    line-height: var(--lh-ui);
  }

  .guides {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
    background: var(--panel);
    border: 1px solid var(--border-panel);
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
  }

  .guide {
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: var(--space-20);
    padding: var(--space-22) var(--space-24);
  }

  .guide + .guide {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }

  .guide-step {
    flex: none;
    width: var(--step-col);
    color: var(--accent);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--fs-ui-sm);
  }

  .guide-text {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-4);
    min-width: 0;
  }

  .guide-title {
    color: var(--text-primary);
    font-size: var(--fs-body);
    font-weight: var(--fw-bold);
    text-decoration: none;
    width: fit-content;
  }

  .guide-title:hover {
    color: var(--accent-hover);
  }

  .guide-title:focus-visible {
    outline: 2px solid var(--accent);
    outline-offset: 3px;
    border-radius: 4px;
  }

  .guide-body {
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-size: var(--fs-ui-sm);
    line-height: var(--lh-ui);
  }

  @media (max-width: 860px) {
    .inner {
      padding: 0 var(--space-20);
    }

    .modules {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    }

    .guide {
      gap: var(--space-14);
    }
  }
</style>
